From: LowBacon <lenni.a.jokitalo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:12:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/25] Memory remapping: locks once per scatter call,
 contiguous pages as one range, no-op remaps skipped; remap lock counters;
 VICTORY_KEYS in release builds (HybridGt)

XMemMapPhysicalPagesScatter took the physical-pages lock and the GPU
side's remapping lock once per page, and each page unmapped and mapped its
view again (four system calls a view, and the GPU side told the range was
new). Texture refreshes read title memory in place under that lock's read
side: run next7 had them wait 740-850 ms in single frames, and the title's
own threads stalled behind it (the card idle 440 ms of a 700 ms frame while
the title had not submitted).

- map_pages: the mapping work under locks the caller holds.
- Scatter: both locks once per call; addresses that follow one another,
  all mapping or all unmapping, are one range (consecutive pages of one
  section become one view, as XMemMapPhysicalPages already did).
- A range that shows the asked pages already is left as it is.
- Counters (frame line): the lock taken, waited for, held; pages; no-ops.
- VICTORY_KEYS works in release builds (it only reads the variable).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
